\par
\b\fs24 Scope\b0\fs22\par
This timeline is built from the current manuscript and the project notes already present in the Scrivener file. It does not try to solve every continuity problem by force. Where the draft gives a clear sequence but unstable dates, this folder preserves the sequence and marks the uncertainty.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Primary date anchors currently visible in the draft\b0\fs22\par
- 2023 [Explicit]: public-history claim that sentients overthrew the United Nations facility at ground zero.\par
- 2024-12-21 [Explicit]: facility terminal entry showing the lost facility as inactive / awaiting decommission.\par
- Circa 2048 [Explicit]: archive-era material in "Ghost's in the sea of shells."\par
- SOL year 2056 / Earth rotation 287 [Explicit, Conflicted]: John's wake-up / briefing date at the start of the main narrative.\par
- 2155 [Explicit, Conflicted]: post-{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://4B07A290-3806-421E-B4FB-1EC8BBD4A105"}{\fldrsltgate}} arrival year announced by Tebo using Oeacion adjustment.\par
- 2174 [Explicit, Conflicted]: one facility system readout during the lost-facility sequence.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Working rule used in this folder\b0\fs22\par
- Pre-{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://1B9B5B70-903C-4803-9B5A-2B1A1CFE7B86"}{\fldrsltgate}} "present day" uses 2056 as the best working anchor, because it is the clearest direct narration date.\par
- 2155 is treated as the post-{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://90227E13-3B63-4C08-8C1E-935565C465B1"}{\fldrsltgate}} / later-era anchor because the manuscript explicitly announces it after transit.\par
- 2174 is treated as unresolved until the manuscript clarifies whether it is a real date, a terminal error, or an older draft remnant.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Best way to use this folder going forward\b0\fs22\par
- Use "01 - Master Lore Timeline" for setting history.\par
- Use "02 - Story Sequence" for chapter order and current plot flow.\par
- Use "03 - Continuity Flags" when revising dates, names or institutional history.\par
